00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.020
So the first project is Intrade.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.230
So Intrade was a website
that you could bet on events.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.900
So how it works is, for
example, if you thought

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.049
Obama was going to
win the election,

00:07:47.049 --> 00:07:48.590
then you have a
marketplace for that.

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:51.890
For example, if the price is
at $9.00 and you buy at $9

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:54.530
and Obama actually
wins the election,

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:56.360
then it will automatically
go up to $10.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.880
So it's $0 to $10.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:00.200
So then you would gain $1.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.260
If he'd lost the election,
it will go to $0.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.370
So that means all the
money invested, the $9

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:08.750
invested, you'll lose it
all and it will become $0.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.060
So basically it's
like a stock market.

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.625
And then also, my
brother told me that, oh,

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:15.071
it's actually a binary option.

00:08:15.071 --> 00:08:16.820
I don't want to bore
you with the details.

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:19.330
But basically, in
a finance world,

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.140
whatever I was playing
with in that website

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.081
